WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.540
SPEAKER: It's officially week
three of the Google Cloud Next

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.380
OnAir, which means we're
focusing on infrastructure.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.620
I'm Priyanka Vergadia, and
welcome to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:14.100
where we're taking a sneak
peek at this week's content.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.450
Week three is all
about infrastructure,

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.810
meaning we want to help
you migrate and modernize,

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:22.050
so we've got tons of
informational sessions

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:24.240
from virtual machines
to networking

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.490
and looking at the details
of cloud environment.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.660
This week is also full of
customer migration stories,

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.390
so you can hear the decisions
that drove companies

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:36.030
to the cloud and how they
planned out their migration

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:37.110
strategy.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:40.530
Let's shine the spotlight on
Proactive Network Operations,

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:44.310
a session that shows off how the
Network Intelligence Center can

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.160
help you monitor, troubleshoot,
and even visualize

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.240
your network.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.700
This session is pretty
cool because whether you're

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:54.120
about to migrate to cloud or
you've been there for years,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.760
network outages are
always concerning,

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.460
so learning to be proactive
with your network operations

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:02.100
is a skill that will
always be valuable.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.010
Fun fact.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:06.540
I'm kind of a cloud nerd, which
is why my playlist has Alerting

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:07.870
Best Practices.

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:10.050
This session will be
a thorough explanation

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.060
of the alerts feature
in Google Cloud

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:15.210
Monitoring and the many ways
you can tweak your alerts

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:17.940
to find meaningful
signals in your data.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:20.640
From aggregation to
filtering and grouping

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.670
and even to aligners,
there's plenty to learn,

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.440
and I can't wait.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.780
To wrap things up, check
out the weekly recap

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:31.630
